            nav: 'Process',
            title: 'From idea to handoff in *development*',
            lead: 'That was the path from formulating the idea to handing the mockups off to development. Below are the key stages and what I did at each.',
            content: ':::flow\ncircle | Idea | The developer described the problems of the employment market and proposed creating an MVP, focusing on real user pain points. We discussed typical job search scenarios and interactions with recruiters, and wrote down the main frustrating factors.\nsquare | Features | Without binding to a specific structure, I formed a pool of features that should simplify the search and make the process more transparent for both sides.\nsquare | Audience | I formulated prototype personas, compiled JTBD and CJM.\nsquare | Competitors | I analyzed solutions from hh.ru, Indeed, LinkedIn and others: I identified their UX weaknesses and good practices that could be adapted.\nsquare | Structure | I composed the structure of user transitions for key scenarios (job search, response, response status), built the basic interface architecture, thought through navigation, screens and their relationships, and created draft wireframes.\nsquare | Design system | I defined the styling, typography, color palette, component states and interaction patterns.\nsquare | Mockups | I drew the screens in the final visualization and assembled a clickable prototype.\ncircle | Handoff | I fixed basic UI guidelines and component logic. Within the MVP the team aimed for fast assembly, so the documentation was minimal but structured.\n:::',
